    if android:
        installation=f'''<h2>Install the phone app.</h2><ol class="prose"><li><strong>Download the debug APK on your phone.</strong><br>The installable asset is <code>PocketMic-v0.1.4-debug.apk</code>. The separate <code>release-unsigned.apk</code> is not the consumer installation path.</li><li><strong>Review the source and Android’s installation prompt.</strong><br>Only allow installation from a source you trust. Do not disable Play Protect or ignore an unexpected warning. This is an early, debug-signed build.</li><li><strong>Open PocketMic and allow microphone access when requested.</strong><br>Install and open the Windows receiver next. Pair only on your trusted private network.</li></ol><div class="callout warning"><strong>Check before you trust.</strong><p>The v0.1.4 release does not include a production-signed Android APK. A checksum helps confirm the downloaded file matches the release; it does not replace publisher trust or a security review.</p></div><h2>Installing from your PC?</h2><p>With Android platform tools and an authorised device already configured, use the published APK:</p><pre><code>adb install -r .\\PocketMic-v0.1.4-debug.apk</code></pre>'''
    else:
        installation=f'''<h2>Start the PC receiver.</h2><ol class="prose"><li><strong>Download and extract the ZIP.</strong><br>Use <code>PocketMicReceiver-win-x64.zip</code> from the same release as the Android app.</li><li><strong>Run <code>PocketMicReceiver.exe</code>.</strong><br>The package is self-contained; the release does not require a separate .NET runtime installation. Review any Windows publisher or security warnings before proceeding.</li><li><strong>Use a trusted private network.</strong><br>Allow only the documented PocketMic traffic on your Private firewall profile. Do not switch off the firewall or port-forward the receiver.</li><li><strong>Pair the Android app and choose an output.</strong><br>For a first direct listening test, use headphones. To expose the audio as a microphone input in another app, install VB-CABLE and choose <code>CABLE Input</code>.</li></ol><div class="callout"><strong>This is a ZIP, not an installer.</strong><p>Extract the full package before running the executable. Automatic updates and a bundled virtual microphone driver are not part of this download.</p></div>'''
    other='windows' if android else 'android'
