    p.body+=f'''<section class="page-section"><div class="wrap body-grid"><article>{installation}<h2>Verify the downloaded file.</h2><p>Compare a SHA-256 hash with the value below or the release’s {ext(SUMS,'SHA256SUMS.txt')}.</p><pre><code>Get-FileHash .\\{name} -Algorithm SHA256</code></pre><p id="release-hash" class="hash">{sha}</p><button class="btn small" type="button" data-copy="release-hash">{icon('copy')} Copy SHA-256</button><dl class="file-details"><div><dt>Release</dt><dd>v0.1.4 · 9 September 2026</dd></div><div><dt>Required counterpart</dt><dd>{'Windows receiver' if android else 'Android app'}</dd></div></dl><h2>Downloaded? Keep going.</h2><p>A download click does not confirm installation. Once the app is installed, get the other half and follow the setup checklist.</p><div class="btn-row">{p.button(other,'Get the '+('Windows receiver' if android else 'Android app'),primary=True)}{p.button('setup','Both installed? Set up')}</div>{p.source_note()}</article><aside><div class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">You’ll also need</p><h2>{'The Windows receiver.' if android else 'The Android app.'}</h2><p>PocketMic is a two-device setup. Use both apps from the same release.</p>{p.button(other,'Get '+('Windows' if android else 'Android'),primary=True)}<hr><h2>For app mic routing</h2><p>VB-CABLE is installed separately. Receiver: <code>CABLE Input</code>. Your app: <code>CABLE Output</code>.</p>{p.link('setup','See the full route '+icon('arrow'),suffix='#route')}</div></aside></div></section>'''

