checks=''.join(f'<div class="check-item" id="step-{id}"><input type="checkbox" id="check-{id}" data-setup-step="{id}" aria-describedby="desc-{id}"><div><h2><label for="check-{id}">{i+1}. {title}</label></h2><p id="desc-{id}">{text}</p></div></div>' for i,(id,title,text) in enumerate(check_data))
routing_details=f'''<details class="routing-detail" data-destination="discord"><summary>Discord: input device + mic test</summary><p>Open <strong>Voice & Video</strong>, choose <code>CABLE Output</code> as the input device, then use <strong>Mic Test</strong> to listen. Leave the output device on your headphones. {ext(DISCORD,'Official Discord guide')}.</p></details><details class="routing-detail" data-destination="obs"><summary>OBS: scene input + test recording</summary><p>Add an <strong>Audio Input Capture</strong> source and select <code>CABLE Output</code>. Avoid capturing the same device globally and in the scene. Record and review a short sample for level and sync. {ext(OBS,'Official OBS guide')}.</p></details><details class="routing-detail" data-destination="meetings"><summary>Teams / calling apps: microphone + test call</summary><p>Choose <code>CABLE Output</code> as the calling app’s microphone. In Teams, use <strong>Settings → Devices</strong> and the audio settings, then make a test call where available. For other apps, use their own input selector and test. {ext(TEAMS,'Official Teams guide')}.</p></details><details class="routing-detail" data-destination="general"><summary>Other Windows apps: select the recording endpoint</summary><p>Choose <code>CABLE Output</code> in the app’s microphone selector where supported. If the endpoint has been renamed, match it to VB-CABLE’s recording side. Test the actual app before relying on it.</p></details>'''
p.body+=f'''<section class="page-section"><div class="wrap body-grid"><article><div class="checklist">{checks}</div><h2 id="route">Input goes in.<br>Output comes out.</h2>{route_flow()}<p>The receiver plays <em>into</em> VB-CABLE through <code>CABLE Input</code>. Your app reads <em>from</em> it through <code>CABLE Output</code>. Those two names are not interchangeable.</p><div class="setup-select"><label for="destination">Show the starting point for my app</label><select id="destination"><option value="general">Another Windows app</option><option value="discord">Discord</option><option value="obs">OBS Studio</option><option value="meetings">Teams / meetings</option></select></div>{routing_details}<div class="callout warning"><strong>Avoid feedback while testing.</strong><p>Keep the receiver’s speaker-monitoring option off when you do not need it. Use headphones for a direct listening test, then check the actual destination app.</p></div><h2>Now listen to the result.</h2><p>Once your destination app can hear you, continue to the final sound-check notes. Only you can confirm whether the native-app setup worked.</p><div class="btn-row"><a id="setup-done" class="btn primary" href="{p.href('ready')}">I can hear it in my app {icon('check')}</a>{p.button('help','Still no sound?')}</div><p class="footnote">Checks are saved only for this browser tab’s session. They are your confirmations, not automated tests. No audio, pairing keys, or device addresses are entered here.</p>{p.source_note('Driver routing follows '+ext(VB,'VB-Audio’s documentation')+'.')}</article><aside><div class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">Setup checklist</p><h2>Your progress.</h2><div class="progress-wrap"><p id="setup-progress-label">0 of 6 steps checked by you</p><progress id="setup-progress" max="6" value="0" aria-labelledby="setup-progress-label"></progress></div><p>This website cannot confirm installation, connection, or sound quality.</p><button class="reset-btn" type="button" id="reset-checklist">Reset this checklist</button><hr>{p.link('downloads','Missing an app? '+icon('arrow'))}<br><br>{p.link('help','Open troubleshooting '+icon('arrow'))}<hr><h2>Network guardrail</h2><p>Trusted Private network only. Use the project’s firewall helper when needed. Never port-forward or disable the firewall to make pairing work.</p></div></aside></div></section>'''

